  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Let me close by collecting the whole walkthrough into four guarantees. First, the bank is charged at most once - that is the service ternary, the idempotency node, and the atomic create working together. Second, we never fake a result - a timeout is unknown, and we say so with a 503 and an INIT record. Third, card data never appears at rest, in responses, or in logs. Fourth, our observability cannot lie, because the audit node guards on terminal states. Every slide you saw maps to a class, and every class maps to a test. I would be glad to go deeper on any of it.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
